WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.479 --> 00:00:06.490
You know, we've been talking about the possibility
that on Election Day, Donald Trump will try

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:12.349
to use federal troops to intimidate voters
at polling places.

00:00:12.349 --> 00:00:17.420
And it turns out that Trump may not even have
to because his own supporters are showing

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:21.699
up at early voting sites and already intimidating
voters.

00:00:21.699 --> 00:00:26.890
We're seeing a big advantage for Democrats
in terms of absentee ballots and in terms

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:28.619
of early voting.

00:00:28.619 --> 00:00:33.280
And the Trump lists are showing up and doing
what they can to intimidate voters.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:40.190
Virginia had its first week of early voting
groups of Trump supporters were showing up,

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:45.490
including in northern Virginia, blocking the
path to the location.

00:00:45.490 --> 00:00:50.379
This was a disproportionately Democratic area
of Virginia chanting four more years.

00:00:50.379 --> 00:00:57.769
It actually led to county election officials
having to provide escorts for voters to get

00:00:57.769 --> 00:01:00.359
past the protesters.

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:05.860
Groups of Trump supporters were chanting four
more years and doing all sorts of other stuff.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:06.950
We have video.

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:11.010
This was captured by Maryland photographer
Anthony Tilghman.

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:15.800
And you'll see the crowd carrying Trump signs,
flags, chanting right outside the building,

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:18.160
making it difficult to get in and out.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:25.400
Now, remember, the legality of this is unclear
because electioneering at polling places isn't

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:26.670
allowed.

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:30.470
What counts as being at the polling place
depends on the state.

00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:34.580
In Virginia, my understanding is that it's
within 40 feet of the front doors.

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:38.780
It certainly seems as though in this video,
the protesters are within 40 feet of the front

00:01:38.780 --> 00:02:13.489
doors.

00:02:13.489 --> 00:02:19.049
So as you can see, trumpet's creating a blockade,
chanting, blocking the path, and now there

00:02:19.049 --> 00:02:22.969
are people who are saying, including the Virginia
Republican Party, which I'll get to.

00:02:22.969 --> 00:02:26.410
There are people saying this is an intimidation.

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:31.420
Only the most triggered snowflake could consider
this intimidation.

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:33.130
Anybody can just walk by.

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:36.540
Guys, this is not how elections are supposed
to happen.

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:39.620
There is not supposed to be electioneering
at polling places.

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:46.329
If you are just to pick something for a 70
year old woman showing up to vote for Biden,

00:02:46.329 --> 00:02:51.340
and you have to weave your way through a crowd
of dozens of Trump trumpets by the front door

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:56.319
chanting, blocking the path, holding signs,
screaming.

00:02:56.319 --> 00:03:00.069
That is not how elections are supposed to
happen in the United States.

00:03:00.069 --> 00:03:06.249
There are election officials in Fairfax County,
Virginia, and who are admitting that voters

00:03:06.249 --> 00:03:10.709
and even some of the poll workers felt intimidated
by this crowd.

00:03:10.709 --> 00:03:16.069
And again, they required escorts to get people
in and out of the building.

00:03:16.069 --> 00:03:18.290
And again, it's illegal in Virginia.

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:22.819
You can't be within 40 feet of the precincts
in Virginia.

00:03:22.819 --> 00:03:27.560
Now, the Virginia Republican Party just mocked
the entire thing.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:32.549
The New York Times put out a story about this
and the Virginia Republican Party tweeted

00:03:32.549 --> 00:03:34.349
the story with the message.

00:03:34.349 --> 00:03:40.810
Quick, someone called the whammed billons,
which is just, you know, the height of maturity.

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:46.830
And interestingly, some of the voters who
were in line to vote were asked, why are you

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:49.569
standing in such a long line to vote in person?

00:03:49.569 --> 00:03:50.939
You could vote by mail.

00:03:50.939 --> 00:03:53.970
You're standing in line to vote early in person.

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:57.299
And voter said, we don't trust the mail.

00:03:57.299 --> 00:03:58.840
Take a look at this report from CNN.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:02.749
I just got to step out here so you can see
just how far back this line goes.

00:04:02.749 --> 00:04:05.230
I mean, it's about two football fields here.

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:09.560
And keep in mind, this is a huge government
building in Fairfax, Virginia, the biggest

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:13.459
county here, and they're at capacity inside
of the building.

00:04:13.459 --> 00:04:16.389
They're trying to keep people here outside
socially distant.

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:21.670
But as you can see, it is difficult, particularly
given the fact that this slide is so enormous.

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:27.020
And once they actually get inside of the building,
there is still at least an hour and a half

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:28.020
wait.

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:32.170
Now, we have talked to several of these voters
about why it is that they chose to show up

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:33.800
early.

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:38.520
Many of them think they knew it was going
to be a very big election, that it was critical

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:40.040
that there was going to be a lot of interest.

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:42.230
They wanted to be one of the first people
to cast their ballot.

00:04:42.230 --> 00:04:46.060
But we also heard about mistrust of the postal
service.

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:58.280
Take a listen to this program on trust, the
real that's out of here all day.

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:04.340
So this gets me to the one good thing that
I am seeing in terms of enthusiasm.

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:05.380
It seems to be high.

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:08.260
I've been using this phrase for a couple of
months.

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:12.080
People might be willing to crawl over broken
glass to vote.

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:14.350
It seems people are willing to do it.

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:19.540
And the death of Ruth Bader Ginsburg tragic
and may lead to one of the most conservative

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:21.040
supreme courts in decades.

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:24.420
But it seems to have increased enthusiasm
on the left.

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:30.760
Donations to Democrats have been pouring in
since the past passing of Ruth Bader Ginsburg.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:36.720
And if anything like this happens when you
are voting, I want to hear about it.

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:38.800
If you can safely take video.

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:41.270
Take video and get it to me.

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:45.060
We will be talking about the voter intimidation
that takes place.

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:46.890
Keep an eye out and let me know what you see

